&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us ...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soho House Amsterdam&lt;/strong&gt; is part of a global community for creative people, offering a welcoming space to work, relax, and connect. Recently awarded a Michelin Key, our House is recognized for its exceptional comfort and design. Join our team and help deliver thoughtful, high-quality experiences for our members and guests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role ...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced and technically capable &lt;strong&gt;Maintenance Technician&lt;/strong&gt; to join the Maintenance team at Soho House Amsterdam.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role for someone with strong practical maintenance experience within a hotel or hospitality environment. The successful candidate will be confident working independently, diagnosing faults, carrying out repairs and taking ownership of maintenance tasks through to completion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with the &lt;strong&gt;Maintenance Manager and wider maintenance team&lt;/strong&gt;, providing technical and operational support across the day-to-day running of the building.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role requires someone who understands the demands of a busy hotel and members&#39; club environment and who is comfortable working across guest rooms, restaurants, kitchens, bars, offices, public areas and technical spaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Main responsibilities&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carry out planned and reactive maintenance throughout the building.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose technical faults and carry out appropriate first-line repairs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carry out general repairs across plumbing, carpentry, basic electrical work and general building maintenance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the maintenance of mechanical equipment, pumps, ventilation and heating/cooling systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carry out regular inspections of plant rooms, guest areas and back-of-house spaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify developing or recurring faults and report recommended solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of assigned maintenance tasks from initial report through to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Maintenance Manager with planned preventative maintenance and follow-up actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the coordination of specialist contractors and service providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure contractor works are completed correctly and identify any outstanding issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support with technical information, quotations and preparation for maintenance works and small projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate records of maintenance work, service reports and outstanding actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with room preventative maintenance programmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support maintenance relating to fire safety systems, water systems, access control and other building services where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor maintenance materials, spare parts and consumables and report when stock needs replenishment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond professionally and efficiently to urgent technical issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Housekeeping, Operations, F&amp;amp;B, Security and other departments to resolve maintenance issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain high standards of workmanship, cleanliness and safety at all times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow all relevant health and safety, fire safety and emergency procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Previous maintenance experience within a hotel or hospitality environment is essential.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong practical experience in general building maintenance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with plumbing, carpentry and basic electrical fault-finding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge or practical experience of HVAC, ventilation and heating/cooling systems would be a strong advantage.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to troubleshoot technical issues and determine the appropriate next steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable recognising when specialist contractor support is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to read technical manuals, service reports and basic technical drawings where required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with external contractors and service companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of planned preventative maintenance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in a busy, guest-facing operational environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to manage multiple maintenance priorities and work independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliable, organised and able to follow tasks through to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong spoken English and good communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional when dealing with guests, colleagues, contractors and suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible to work evenings and weekends when equired.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📍 Amsterdam | 🛠️ Hands-on work, varied tasks, and a collaborative environment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re practical, reliable, and take pride in keeping things running smoothly behind the scenes, we’d love to hear from you!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
